    "C": "Explore a distinct horizontal-first streaming formulation rather than assuming the existing row-band variants provide parallel gains. For each input row, compute M=N-S+1 width-S sums in 64-bit arithmetic. Maintain vertical totals for those M positions, adding incoming filtered values and subtracting expiring ones; after S rows, reduce their maximum. Retain only filtered rows that will expire, using min(S,N-S)*M 64-bit history entries. This makes vertical updates and maxima independent SIMD lanes, but moves horizontal scanning to every input row and changes memory traffic, so compare end-to-end against existing programs. Keep the existing coarse row-band implementation as a separate contender only if the unchanged build actually enables OpenMP; cap it at the four available cores and preserve a serial path.",
