    "analysis": "Only Problem B matches the supplied source. The baseline is 0.125845 s; admissible O(N²) programs range from 0.054076 to 0.055941 s. B's NEON program is provisionally fastest, approximately 2.33× baseline, but A's streaming ring is only 0.62% slower and C's simpler bands only 0.96% slower. Candidate variability is unavailable, so these rankings are not conclusive. Every candidate still uses scanf per matrix element, making input conversion a strong untested bottleneck hypothesis. ARM64 supports the NEON direction; guarded OpenMP code alone does not establish that threading was active. Preserve 64-bit intermediates and maxima initialized from actual windows for all valid inputs."
